{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pulls/70","id":4977734150,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSLn-hc8AAAABKLIyBg","html_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pull/70","diff_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pull/70.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pull/70.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/issues/70","number":70,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Deliver queued data for paused child stream reads","user":{"login":"codexcoder21","id":216437543,"node_id":"U_kgDODOaTJw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216437543?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21","html_url":"https://github.com/codexcoder21","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"During the 2026-10-22 test campaign, the owner asked: \"Your goal is to add end-to-end integration tests which identify bugs (the tests should initially fail), and then fix the bug in the implementation.\" Moving UrlProtocol to snapshot-38 in https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/846 left `testGossipServiceQueryResponseFlushesUnderBackpressure` failing at its unchanged 30-second limit because `read()` on a paused child did not deliver queued data. This fixes the upstream behavior described in https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/issues/62.\n\nAn explicit read now delivers one queued payload and read-complete while auto-read remains disabled, or waits for the next payload. Pending requests coalesce. Callback reads continue without nested callbacks, and Mplex re-arms its paused transport after a resume callback requests more data. The child config handles automatic resume separately so a delayed automatic read cannot be mistaken for explicit demand. Existing receive limits, receive-credit accounting, EOF order and close cleanup remain in effect.\n\nValidation:\n- Real TCP/Noise reproduction failed for both Mplex and Yamux before the fix. All 11 initial new cases failed their first runtime baseline attempt.\n- Review added an empty-queue callback case: Mplex initially failed because the second physical payload never arrived; the correction re-arms after clearing the drain guard.\n- All 13 new cases plus 68 neighbour cases passed on the first attempt in three fresh runs: 81/81 each. Coverage includes 8,000 concurrent pre-arrival reads, one-byte transport reads, EOF, callback close, receive bounds, backing storage, sibling progress and connection teardown.\n- Formatting, static analysis and library assembly pass. The formatter also updates the newly merged capacity callback test's wrapping and branch braces; its conditions and assertions are preserved.\n- Three bounded full-suite acquisitions (90, 10 and 9 minutes, with later attempts following actual holder changes) all exited before Gradle started. The final timestamp audit found zero fresh reports and rejected 25 stale targeted XML files. Total actual full-suite executions: zero. The suite and comparison with the known 20 baseline failures remain unverified, so this PR stays draft. Memory was sampled; no test suite was killed or retried.\n- The required Kotlin check https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/runs/120247035520 is completed/success on this exact head. Its summary says no build.kts was found, so it ran no Gradle build or tests. A fresh watch-only build-watchman exited GREEN/0. Actions startup failures remain the known repository condition. The earlier zero-dispatch hold is resolved; this lane performed no receiver change or rerequest.\n\nIndependent test and implementation review: https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/blob/wip/JL62-evidence-20261023/lane-evidence/JL62-review.md . Baseline failures, full stacks, run summaries and findings: https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/tree/wip/JL62-evidence-20261023/lane-evidence . No timeout or iteration changes, mocks, reflection, merge, publication or deployment.\n\nRemaining verification is tracked in https://www.handoff.wasmserver.com/handoffs/hf-2026-10-23-finish-full-suite-and-ci-verification-for-paused-child-manual-reads. The dispatch dependency is resolved; the local full-suite gate remains.\n\nCloses https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/issues/62\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-10-23T04:17:23Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T05:10:57Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"3589d21d3685180f47b743e3037fd0d90eb93a3b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pulls/70/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pulls/70/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/issues/70/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/statuses/091b6d17280045ec2a1260ec890d1a06991bb6ac","head":{"label":"CodexCo